---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";

//image compression
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import hero from "../images/hero/hero2.jpg";
import excursions from "../images/media/excursions.jpg";

//icons
import { Icon } from "astro-icon";

const {
  title,
  charset,
  description,
  canonical,
  noindex,
  nofollow,
  openGraph,
  languageAlternates,
  extend,
} = Astro.props;
---

<MainLayout
  lang="en"
  pageIndex="excursions"
  pageIndexEn="excursions"
  title="Excursions | Elamio Yachting"
  charset={charset}
  description="Check out premade excursions set up just for you | Elamio Yachting"
  canonical={canonical}
  openGraph={openGraph}
  extend={extend}
  noindex
  nofollow
>
  <div class="hero_content txtOnDark txt-center flex-center">
    <div class="black"></div>
    <Image
      src={excursions}
      alt="boat"
      format="avif"
      loading="lazy"
      class="hero-img"
    />
    <div class="heroContainer-default">
      <h1 class="h1 clr-main-light">Excursions</h1>

      <h2 class="body clr-main-light">Let's get on the boat right away</h2>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- about -->
  <div class="section txtOnDark center txt-center flex-columns wrapper">
    <div class="flex-left boat-text-l">
      <h2 class="h2">About</h2>
      <div class="line-acc-full mart-200"></div>
      <p class="body padt-200 padb-200">
        All trips are tailor-made according to our guest’s wish list and their
        preferences. We, at Elamio yachting, are all about the experience and
        high-quality service which is why everything is planned thoroughly to
        ensure that every detail is personalized and unique just for you! It’s
        all about creating the perfect experience tailored to your preferences
        and interests.
      </p>
      <a href="#trips"><div class="btnFill marb-200">VIEW ALL</div></a>
    </div>

    <div class="flex-right">
      <Image
        src={excursions}
        alt="vis"
        format="avif"
        loading="lazy"
        class="flex-img hidden-fade"
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section wrapper txtOnDark center" id="trips">
    <h2 class="h2 clr-prim-acc padb-200">Vis</h2>
    <p class="body justify">
      Visiting this military island means creating memories for a lifetime.
      Island of Vis served as a naval and military base back in Yugoslavia.
      Therefore, the island has remained preserved and wild. Exploring its
      military tunnels, hidden coves and the jewel for itself, Blue Cave, will
      make your day on this island one of a kind.
    </p>
    <button class="accordion">Itinerary</button>
    <div class="panel">
      <p class="body">
        We are leaving Split around 10:00AM, from where we are headed towards
        island of Vis. On our way there; you will be enjoying views of Brač and
        Šolta while getting some tan or enjoying sipping your drink in the
        shade. Our first stop will be Blue Cave where we are going to tie to a
        buoy, which is a perfect time to have a swim while awaiting a chauffeur
        to take you to the Cave. Upon return to the boat, the tour continues
        cruising along southern side of Vis giving you the opportunity to see
        military tunnels and magnificent cliffs Vis abounds with. En-route we
        will visit places where ''Mamma Mia'' was shot, as well as stopping in
        mesmerizing Stiniva cove for swimming and tanning before lunch. There is
        a paddle board available on the boat for the ones who would like to have
        a little exercise right before lunch. Once everyone's back on the boat,
        we will cruise towards the beautiful lagoon with crystal clear water by
        the little island of Budihovac. We are suggesting having a lunch at a
        unusual restaurant that is overlooking the entire lagoon. Everything you
        can eat in the restaurant is fresh and grown on that little island of
        Budihovac. While eating lunch you can enjoy the beautiful views hidden
        in the shade of Mediterranean trees and having domestic animals walking
        around this wild oasis. This spot is perfect for snorkeling, swimming
        and paddle boarding after lunch, due to its shallow turquoise water.
        Once everyone is ready to go back, you will be enjoying relaxing ride
        watching sunset on our way back to home port where we get around 6:00PM.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section wrapper txtOnDark center" id="trips">
    <h2 class="h2 clr-prim-acc padb-200">Šolta and Blue Lagoon</h2>
    <p class="body justify">
      Island of Šolta is a perfect spot for a relaxing day on the boat. Its
      secluded beaches, hidden coves and turquoise water are all that is needed
      for a summer adventure. On the other hand, Blue Lagoon is really what its
      name represents. Shallow crystal clear water will make you want jump on a
      paddle board and paddle all around the lagoon which will take your breath
      away.
    </p>
    <button class="accordion">Itinerary</button>
    <div class="panel">
      <p class="body">
        Departure from Split should be around 10:00AM, from which we are headed
        to Maslinica, typical Dalmatian little village that has a rich history.
        It is mostly known for its Martinis Marchi castle which was built at the
        beginning of the 18th century to defend the village from constant pirate
        attacks. We will have a stop there, so you could go for a walk,
        sightseeing or just have a good morning coffee while enjoying the
        beautiful scenery. Afterwards, the tour continues towards Blue lagoon
        where we will be having lunch at a local restaurant overlooking the
        crystal clear water of the Blue Lagoon. The lagoon is a perfect sport
        for swimming, snorkeling, and paddle boarding, both before and after
        lunch. In the late afternoon hours we will slowly cruise towards home
        port of Split while soaking up the last rays of sun and having a glass
        of Croatian wine to seize the day. Arrival to Split is expected to be
        around 7:00PM.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section wrapper txtOnDark center" id="trips">
    <h2 class="h2 clr-prim-acc padb-200">Hvar and Pakleni islands</h2>
    <p class="body justify">
      Hvar has been one of the most popular summer destinations for years,
      mostly to its charm, not many can resist to. Pakleni islands archipelago
      which sits right in front of port of Hvar rounds it off in a perfect whole
      that just takes your breath away. No wonder Hvar has been on the ‘’to go
      list’’ for many people from all around the world.
    </p>
    <button class="accordion">Itinerary</button>
    <div class="panel">
      <p class="body">
        The adventure starts around 10:00AM from Split. Relaxing on the sundeck
        and enjoying views of Brač and Šolta will be a good way to start the day
        while cruising towards island of Hvar. Upon arrival to a exquisite town
        of Hvar, you will be able to have a walk around the town, climb to a
        fortress which sits on top of the hill, or just maybe go shopping or
        have a coffee. Once you are ready to cool off, we will be heading to
        Pakleni islands through narrow passages and coves which are all perfect
        for swimming, sunbathing and snorkeling. One of them stands out; It is
        Palmižana which is known worldwide for crystal clear water, great lounge
        bars and restaurants located in botanical gardens. After exploring this
        amazing archipelago, we will get going towards the Southern side of the
        island where we will show you mesmerizing cove of Dubovica and take you
        swimming in front of fascinating Red Rocks. Eventually, we continue
        towards hidden cove of Milna where we will tie onto a buoy from which
        the restaurant chauffer will take you to the restaurant which is owned
        by a local fisherman. The restaurant sits right by the water with
        splendid views of the offing, cliffs and sunsets. After lunch you can
        explore the hidden cove of Milna or simply enjoy on the boat and toast
        to life! In the late afternoon hours we will be heading back to Split
        and you will have the opportunity to soak up the beauty of Croatian
        sunsets. Arrival to Split is expected to be around 7:00PM.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section wrapper txtOnDark center" id="trips">
    <h2 class="h2 clr-prim-acc padb-200">Brac</h2>
    <p class="body justify">
      Besides being famous for its olive oil and stone, Brač is home to one of
      the most beautiful beaches in the world; The Golden Horn. Its triangular
      shape with a prominent peak in the sea, the direction which depends on the
      direction of the current and crystal clear water, is something that will
      definitely take your breath.
    </p>
    <button class="accordion">Itinerary</button>
    <div class="panel">
      <p class="body">
        The tour starts around 10AM. While enjoying views of Split from the
        offing we will be heading to our first stop. Little town of Milna is the
        safest harbor on the island and a typical Dalmatian village, perfect for
        a coffee, little walk around the village or capturing memories before
        heading further. Upon return to the boat we are going to go for a swim.
        A hidden cove nearby surrounded with woods and crickets chirping will be
        your spot for cooling off after a nice walk. Afterwards we will be
        heading to Bol, home of the Golden Horn. On our way there you will be
        able to soak up the sun rays while having a glass of cold beverage as
        long as we are driving along the mesmerizing Southern side of Brač. In
        Bol we will be having lunch in a local tavern known for its fish
        delicacies overlooking the island of Hvar on the other side. After
        lunch, there will be plenty of time for swimming, sunbathing, snorkeling
        and (wind) surfing on shores of the Golden Horn. Once everybody is set
        we continue back to Split enjoying a view of a splendid sunset. The
        arrival is scheduled to be around 19:30PM.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section wrapper txtOnDark center" id="trips">
    <h2 class="h2 clr-prim-acc padb-200">Airport Transfer</h2>
    <p class="body justify">
      In case you want to have more time enjoying in beauties of the Adriatic
      coast before heading back home, we will be happy to give you a ride.
      Transfer directly to the airport or simply from point A to point B
      somewhere in between the islands are something our fast boats are perfect
      for!
    </p>
  </div>
</MainLayout>

<script>
  import "../scripts/accordion.js";
</script>
